WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
North Korea

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.134
firing an

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.869
intercontinental ballistic missile

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.504
that flew for more than 70 minutes.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.805
That is the longest missile

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.907
flight ever for North Korea.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:08.641
Kim Jong un,

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.477
they say personally guided the test

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:11.344
firing of the missile.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.212
That is according to North

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.747
Korean state media.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.215
The launch coming just days

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:16.549
after Kim Jong un's sister

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.651
vowed retaliation over an alleged U.S.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:19.786
spy plane.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:21.021
Which they say flew over North

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:22.155
Korean territory.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.924
Will Ripley is OUTFRONT

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.395
A menacing milestone for North Korea's

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:29.496
missile program.

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:32.065
Pyongyang's latest ICBM launch

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.800
breaking its own record

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.835
for the longest ever missile flight.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:39.139
A staggering 74 minutes hurtling

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:40.140
high above the earth

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.276
at supersonic speed, hitting 6000

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:44.878
kilometers before splashing

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.413
down in the sea.

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.313
The massive missiles

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:50.350
potential striking range, the entire U.S.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.652
mainland and most of the world.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.120
Pyongyang's most provocative

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.622
launch in months,

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.157
coinciding with this NATO's

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.591
summit in Lithuania,

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.427
quickly condemned by Japan

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.729
as an unacceptable threat

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.230
to regional stability.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:04.831
South Korea's

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.600
military ready to overwhelmingly respond.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.002
The ICBM,

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.437
a crown jewel in leader

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.305
Kim Jong un's nuclear arsenal,

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.873
protecting the power, fortune

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.142
and future of the ruling Kim family.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:17.644
His young daughter, Kim Ju

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:20.046
a often appearing alongside her dad,

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.481
barely ten years

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.616
old, the rising star of a state

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.418
propaganda campaign

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.153
carefully crafted by Kim's

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.188
younger sister,

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:30.690
the mastermind of the Kim family brand.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.759
The leader's loyal confidante,

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.127
trusted adviser,

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.362
and perhaps the most powerful woman

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.630
in North Korea.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.799
She is the number two war.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.067
That is for sure.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:43.436
But actually, she is very smart lady

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:46.172
and she actually knows

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.208
that her position is secure

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:51.177
only when her brother is secure

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:52.979
just five years ago.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:55.381
Very few people knew of Kim Yo Jong.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.750
She stepped on the South Korean soil,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.219
the first member of North

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:01.821
Korea's ruling family to cross the DMZ.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.790
She carried a message of peace

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.158
from Pyongyang,

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:07.427
North Korean athletes and cheer squads.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:08.161
We got a warm

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:10.263
welcome at the 2018 Winter Olympics.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.465
She rose to fame as a fixture

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:13.800
at her brother's side.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.468
Standing silently behind Kim

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.337
as he met with former President Trump.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:17.937
That brief

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.172
period of diplomacy

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:21.241
feels like a distant memory.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.876
The silent sister, now

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.878
a loud voice of defiance,

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.347
issuing fiery statements on state media,

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.883
often laced with crude language.

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:30.483
This week,

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.619
she threatened to shoot down U.S.

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:33.853
spy planes

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:34.621
accusing them

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:36.156
without evidence of entering

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.423
North Korean territory.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:39.392
Warning in case of repeated

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.327
illegal intrusions, the U.S.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:42.695
forces will experience

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.797
a very critical flight.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:47.400
Past actions proved she's not all talk.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:48.434
In 2020

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.903
a dispute with South Korea

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.538
ended with a bang.

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:53.006
Kim ordered the demolition

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:55.141
of a joint liaison office at the border.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.443
Turning diplomatic dreams

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.912
into a pile of rubble.

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:04.184
She blew up that building

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.219
because she was angry about activists

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:09.122
sending balloons with leaflets

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:10.657
that oppose the regime.

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:11.491
That was her response.

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.759
Let's blow up the building.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:13.660
And she is the second

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.994
most powerful person

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:15.828
in this nation

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:18.231
that has a ever growing nuclear arsenal.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:19.432
And yet she's

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.267
the one that says the US is hostile

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.101
and aggressive.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.036
She called South Korea's

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.871
president a fool recently.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.507
And now that the Washington declaration

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:28.241
will strengthen

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:29.609
the military alliance between the U.S.

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:30.210
and South Korea,

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:34.013
we can expect a lot more from her

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:35.148
Oh, all right.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.549
Thank you very much, Will Ripley.

